      <activity id="8a30c905-48f8-5ec6-bdca-98657a6acec1" activityNameId="b75435be-fc65-5497-8d94-9e40e8e80e38" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Roundwood, azobe (SFM), debarked, u=30%, CM, at maritime harbour</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Roundwood, azobe (SFM), debarked, u=30%, CM, at maritime harbour
data refers to wood from Central Africa, used in Europe. Main ports in Europe include Rotterdam, Hamburg, Bremerhafen or Antwerpen.;
Synonyms: Bongassi, Ekki, Lophira alata; 
UUID: 2ddafd19-a55e-3a51-951f-22cc7b91f912
includes debarking and natural decomposition of the bark, transportation of the log to a main harbour in Europe by truck and freight ship 
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: high technological standard for debarking; average processes for transportation to Europe; transport distance however can vary. high technological standard and legal operations cannot be assumed to be representative for azobe harvesting.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: see Geography
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2ddafd19-a55e-3a51-951f-22cc7b91f912.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="20a9bf48-6cea-59b4-ad08-000cb981f2d0" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
